      "call_source": "transcript_item",
      "params_digest": "a1d2d7d5dd7ae3f6",
      "query": "{\"content\": \"P(grant) is 0.35.\\n\\nThe petition presents a classic Section 1983 *Monell* issue regarding whether a municipality can be held liable for the constitutional torts of an independent contractor healthcare provider on a \\\"nondelegable duty\\\" theory or by automatically treating the provider as a final policymaker. The petition identifies a deep circuit split, with the Fourth, Seventh, and Eleventh Circuits recognizing liability based on the mere delegation of healthcare duties, while the",
