    {
      "call_source": "transcript_item",
      "params_digest": "82578b3fd3643b74",
      "query": "{\"content\": \"Distributed twice so far (effectively its first consideration with full briefing at the September 2026 Long Conference, as it was pulled from its initial conference for a requested response). Expect one further relist before a decision on the petition. The questions presented highlight a clean circuit split over municipal liability for independent healthcare contractors under Section 1983, and the Fourth Circuit's explicit reliance on a \\\"nondelegable duty\\\" theory provides a strong",
